³   REQUIREMENTS -
³
|       386 or higher (a lot higher!) computer.
|       Math coprocessor. YOU can do the thinking otherwise.
:       About 1.7 mb of free *EMS* + about 620k of free base memory.
.       VESA compatible video card with 1 Mb of memory.
        SB or GUS or any other card with wires going to your audio system.

      * This demo was designed to work best with 488DX2-66
      * To get maximum memory available for the demo, run pure EMM386/QEMM
        without Smartdrv, GMouse, etc, etc, etc (preferably QEMM).
      * If you are a lucky owner of 486DX-33 and Sound Blaster, we strongly
        recommend not to run the demo with sampling rate more than 22KHz.
      * Some parts of our demo use high-resolution VESA modes, therefore if
        your computer is known as a trouble-maker in this field, then run
        UNIVBE or any program which installs VESA driver v1.2+.




